WEBVTT

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.510
Kingdom (Part 1)

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.770
COMFY

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.770
Wow!

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.020
Rei.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.520
Good luck at
the Newcomer Tournament finals tomorrow.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:51.780
And so...

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.280
Here. Pork Cut'let's win!

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.280
PORK CUT'LET'S WIN

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:58.280
TA-DAA

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.410
Thank you for the—

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:06.620
Delicious!

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.920
It's crispy!

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.540
And juicy!

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:13.920
Momo's cutlet
is cut in cubes.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.750
Yummy!

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:15.300
I know, right?

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:18.930
I cracked a raw egg
on top of the hot pork cutlet.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.600
So you're going to Osaka tomorrow?

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.850
For events like that,
you arrive the day before, right?

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:30.860
Yes. The Kansai Shogi Hall has
a few rooms available, so I'll be staying there.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:35.070
And Hina, your bullet train leaves
at eight tomorrow, right?

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.150
You have to be at school by seven?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.570
NOM NOM

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:40.570
You have an early morning,
so why don't I draw the bath?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.700
Uh, okay.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.200
Hina, buy me a souvenir!

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.210
Sure.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:55.260
<i>That's right.
Hina's school trip is from tomorrow.</i>

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.930
<i>Two nights and three days in Kyoto.</i>

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.480
Thank you for dinner.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:13.360
Oh, what's wrong? You're done already?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:19.610
I don't know what it is, but my stomach hurts.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.870
Are you all right? Maybe it was too greasy.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:29.620
It's unusual for you to have a stomachache.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.130
Want some medicine?

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:37.420
Yeah.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:48.350
Hina, that's...

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.850
You said your stomach hurts?

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:00.570
There. Lie on your right side.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:04.450
Warming your back like this
may make you feel a little better.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:07.450
Yeah. Thank you.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.410
<i>Is she sick?</i>

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.830
HMM
HMM

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.080
<i>Are you okay, Hina?</i>

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.380
<i>When I thought about her situation at school,</i>

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.880
<i>I can imagine how this three-day,
two-night trip would be painful.</i>

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.680
<i>It was plain as day.</i>

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:36.860
Are you okay?
You know, you don't have to go to Kyoto.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.740
No, I'll go.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:46.450
I have a feeling that I need to go.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.120
It feels like if I don't,

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:59.500
I'll regret it down the line, years from now,
even after becoming an adult.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:09.640
<i>I think I wanted to have memories
of not running away.</i>

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:14.270
<i>So, I can't explain it well,</i>

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.230
<i>but you wanted
to get rid of things like that, right?</i>

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:24.950
<i>That one time,
Takahashi immediately said he understood.</i>

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.040
Hina...

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.540
I'm going to win.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.960
I swear I'll win.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:44.970
<i>Nikaidou kept playing until he collapsed.</i>

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.180
<i>And the girl in front of me...</i>

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.720
<i>...is also fighting.</i>

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.070
I swear I'll win before I come home.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.070
When your stomach feels better,
let's all go to a sweets shop.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.030
You can have whatever toppings you like.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:16.920
Thank you, Kiriyama.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:24.130
<i>They're all fighting to win...</i>

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.890
<i>...their one little place in the world.</i>

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.120
Huh? Where am I?

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:01.670
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:04.630
<i>It's Osaka.</i>

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:11.550
<i>I came here to fight.</i>

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.440
<i>The Newcomer Tournament
is open to shogi players who are 26 and under,</i>

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.520
<i>and 5th dan and under.</i>

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.780
<i>Each player is given five hours.</i>

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:35.740
<i>The match will probably continue
until night time.</i>

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.290
<i>To be on the safe side, I'll buy breakfast, lunch,</i>

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.380
<i>and plenty of drinks.</i>

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.840
Kiriyama is coming today, right?

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.800
Yeah. He's the guy who made our Hachi cry.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:55.350
It's too bad what happened to that rich kid,
but Yamazaki was going all out, too.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:08:02.060
Yeah. After all, his unprecedented title
of "Eternal Newcomer King" was on the line!

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:05.690
You can't blame him.
Maintaining your health is part of the game.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:08.280
Doing everything you can
to beat your opponent,

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.650
no matter what condition they're in,
is just etiquette.

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:13.780
Junkei just fought
the way you're supposed to fight.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:21.460
<i>I suddenly recall what he said.</i>

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.210
<i>I'll have my shot at the title.</i>

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:28.130
<i>If I didn't think that, how could I go on?</i>

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:34.840
<i>I wonder how strongly Nikaidou felt...</i>

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.640
<i>when he said those words.</i>

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.500
You're not mistaken, Rei Kiriyama.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.130
Look to nature for the way of life.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.130
This is the final match
of the Newcomer Tournament.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:14.880
I'm Junkei Yamazaki.

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:18.890
SHOGI HALL

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:41.790
<i>It's quiet.</i>

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:50.050
<i>Only the sound of our pieces disturbs the air.</i>

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.010
<i>He's gunning for a Ranging Rook Castle.</i>

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:05.140
<i>He'll lock himself in,
and intend to make this a drawn-out war.</i>

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:11.940
<i>While playing...</i>

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.240
<i>the question "Why?"...</i>

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:20.740
<i>keeps swirling around in my head.</i>

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.670
<i>When I looked at the game records, I sensed it.</i>

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:31.040
<i>You had plenty of moves that were open.</i>

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:39.720
<i>So why did you force a draw
by repeating moves?</i>

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:46.140
<i>Because I didn't have a winning move.</i>

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:50.690
<i>You can't blame him.
Maintaining your health is part of the game.</i>

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:52.860
<i>Doing everything you can
to beat your opponent,</i>

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.240
<i>no matter what condition they're in,
is just etiquette.</i>

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:58.200
<i>Junkei just fought
the way you're supposed to fight.</i>

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:04.080
<i>The guys in the store said
he fought the way you're supposed to fight.</i>

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.620
<i>But if you're not conquering your weakness
of failing to read your opponent,</i>

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.630
<i>and then you would put that burden
on someone else saying it's justified,</i>

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:18.130
<i>then I have just one reply.</i>

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:32.020
Kingdom (Part 1)

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.100
<i>Go to hell!</i>

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:40.070
<i>Two eyeballs in the dark.</i>

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.620
<i>They're examining my situation.</i>

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.670
<i>Waiting for me to make a mistake.</i>

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.380
<i>Waiting with bated breath...</i>

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:00.630
<i>for the moment I make a wrong move.</i>

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:12.810
<i>He waits patiently.</i>

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:20.950
<i>Like a shadow...</i>

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:24.070
<i>that I can't shake off.</i>

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:28.830
Kingdom 2

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:39.090
<i>In that case, I'll show you.</i>

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.970
<i>Whether I make a mistake or not...</i>

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:50.730
<i>I'll fling all of that mud away!</i>

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.070
<i>Don't try to act cool, Kiriyama!</i>

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:03.570
<i>If you really want to win, then persevere!</i>

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.490
<i>Don't just attack, you have to defend!</i>

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.830
<i>I finally caught up to you, Kiriyama.</i>

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.840
<i>I'll be waiting for the day
when we have a match together.</i>

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:18.840
<i>Right, rival?</i>

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.630
<i>Kiriyama, can you hear me?</i>

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:25.090
ROOK

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.090
<i>Take better care of your shogi,</i>

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:28.100
<i>and yourself, Kiriyama!</i>

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:01.960
<i>I'm always like this.</i>

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:06.090
<i>Bravery and recklessness
are similar but different!</i>

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:13.060
<i>I'm always so quick to focus on myself.</i>

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:18.980
<i>Thanks, Rei.
I should be okay for the next one.</i>

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:26.490
<i>Other people's kindness, strength...</i>

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:32.240
<i>I would probably
be cleaning up by myself and crying.</i>

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:35.870
<i>and loneliness.</i>

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:38.580
<i>I never...</i>

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:31.850
<i>I could never notice it.</i>

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:42.190
<i>It was frustrating.</i>

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:50.030
<i>I felt so pathetic.</i>

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:02.920
Look to nature for the way of life.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:15.180
Newcomer Tournament
Finals

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.180
Idiot.

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:17.850
You really worried me there.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:22.230
You did it. You did it, Kiriyama!

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:26.440
Yes. Yes, it was brilliant.

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:30.650
As expected from your dear rival,
Master Harunobu.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:35.450
SHOGI HALL

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:38.450
KANSAI SHOGI HALL

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.450
Thank you for everything.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.250
Goodbye.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.960
It really works! Shimada 8th-Dan
gave me this stomach medicine.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:50.220
Can I see? I've got stomach pain too.

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:56.810
It really works! When you have a stomachache
because of nerves, consult Shimada 8th-Dan.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.600
He's the authority on stomach pain.

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:04.310
Um, can I see that?

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.020
What, Kiriyama? You have stomach pains, too?

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:09.780
STOMACH
MEDICINE

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:09.780
Want some?

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:12.530
Keep it. I've got plenty.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:19.660
Whoa, hey, Kiriyama!
Before that, congratulations!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.290
You're the Newcomer King!

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.170
Uh... huh?

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:25.420
Kiriyama?

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.430
<i>Suddenly the only thing I could think about</i>

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:42.890
<i>was Hinata, curled up like a little ball
on the floor the night before last.</i>

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:46.440
To the Parents
School Trip Schedule

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:49.190
Kiyomizu Temple
Heian Temple
Lunch
Free Time (Shinkyougoku)
Ginkakuji
Dinner

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:51.190
<i>Kyoto Station is just one stop away
with the bullet train!</i>

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:53.570
<i>Will I make it?</i>

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:57.700
<i>No, I'll go.</i>

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:01.240
<i>I have a feeling that I need to go.</i>

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.960
<i>It feels like if I don't,</i>

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:16.340
<i>I'll regret it down the line, years from now,
even after becoming an adult.</i>

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:21.810
To Shinkyougoku!

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:36.990
GIFT SHOP

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:38.490
NISHIKI TENMANGUU

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.710
UMINO SHOP

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.090
Damn it!

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.630
She's not here?

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:56.930
<i>Of course she's not.</i>

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:01.350
<i>Like I could find a middle school student
who doesn't have a phone</i>

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:05.350
KYOTO GIFTS

00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:05.350
<i>in a town I barely know
by running around randomly,</i>

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:09.940
<i>with "free time in Shinkyougoku"
as my only hint.</i>

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:15.820
<i>What the hell am I doing?</i>

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:18.860
What should I do?

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.740
- I can't make up my mind.
- I know, right?

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.200
Oh, no way, that's totally cute!

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:26.250
<i>Hina's middle school uniform.</i>

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:31.000
<i>Hey, where's Kiriyama?</i>

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.880
<i>I don't know. It's fine, right?</i>

00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:37.760
<i>This is our free time.
So he's free to do what he wants.</i>

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.180
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:44.010
<i>I remember.</i>

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:46.390
<i>Not "here."</i>

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:50.310
<i>Among this laughter,</i>

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:54.570
<i>someone who's all alone won't be found.</i>

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:59.450
<i>She couldn't be here.</i>

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:09.330
<i>That's right.</i>

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:15.090
<i>Whenever she feels like crying,</i>

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:20.760
<i>she heads for the river...</i>

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:28.680
<i>by herself.</i>

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:18.320
Rei?

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:23.530
How?!

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:26.910
Why? What are you doing here?

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:27.990
How?!

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:32.460
Um... Well, uh, let's see...

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:35.920
You said your stomach hurt,

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.920
so I was wondering if you were okay.

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:42.340
So... Oh! That's right.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:46.970
A colleague gave me
a very effective stomach medicine, so...

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:02.440
H-Hina.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:19.090
Hina, you've been hanging in there.
I'm proud of you.

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:25.510
<i>Hina loudly burst into tears</i>

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:28.510
<i>and didn't stop.</i>

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:31.310
<i>She got warmer and warmer.</i>

00:22:32.930 --> 00:22:35.390
<i>Her uniform and head became sweaty.</i>

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:40.020
<i>The breeze off the river
on this slightly cloudy day was chilly,</i>

00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:45.570
<i>so I was worried she would catch a cold.</i>

00:22:45.820 --> 00:22:47.030
<i>I was worried...</i>

00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:50.700
<i>just so worried...</i>

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:54.410
<i>that I couldn't help it.</i>

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.040
Kingdom (Part 2)

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.810
Episode 32

00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:34.300
I thought maybe it was a dream.

00:24:35.060 --> 00:24:38.730
I was in a strange town, all alone,

00:24:38.730 --> 00:24:42.270
feeling lonely, and about to cry,

00:24:42.900 --> 00:24:47.440
you came running over, out of breath,
and with wind-tousled hair,

00:24:48.030 --> 00:24:50.030
and stood before me.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:59.040
ILLUSTRATION:
MINEO MAYA

00:24:50.610 --> 00:24:52.950
School trips bring back memories!

00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:54.120
And when I think of Kyoto,

00:24:54.120 --> 00:24:56.120
I think of tea,
mochi shops, and Yatsuhashi!

00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:58.540
Oh, I can't stop thinking about it!
